  "result": "Perfect! All 215 tests pass. I've successfully added customer statement functionality:\n\n## What was added:\n\n**src/statements.js** \u2014 New module with `statement(customerId, invoices, asOf)` function:\n- Returns `ok({ customerId, invoices, totalDue })`\n- Filters invoices to include only:\n  - Matching customer ID (normalized to uppercase)\n  - Status 'issued' or 'partially_paid'\n  - issueDate on or before asOf date\n- Returns `CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND` for unknown customers\n- For each invoice, returns: `{ number, issueDate, dueDate, total, due }`\n  - `due` calculated using `balanceDue()` from payments module\n  - `dueDate` returned as null if not set\n- Sorts invoices by issueDate (ascending)\n- Calculates `totalDue` as sum of all due amounts\n- Normalizes customer IDs consistently\n\n**test/statements.test.js** \u2014 24 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Customer validation (unknown customer returns CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND)\n- Invoice filtering by status (issued, partially_paid only)\n- Invoice filtering by date (on or before asOf)\n- Customer ID normalization and filtering\n- Sorting by issueDate\n- Field inclusion (number, issueDate, dueDate, total, due)\n- Due amount calculations (full and partial payments)\n- Total due summation\n- Voucher inclusion in totals\n- Multiple customers and payment states\n\nAll 215 tests pass with no regressions.",
